# Edge-case perft suite (the classic Martin Sedlak positions).
#
# Every line targets ONE specific bug class. These are small and fast, but they
# catch the mistakes that the six standard positions miss - and each of these
# bugs, left in, means playing or accepting an illegal move in a real game.
#
# Run: ./chessengine perft suite tests/perft/tricky.epd
#
# When one fails, the comment above it tells you exactly which rule you broke.

# --- en passant legality -----------------------------------------------------
# Capturing en passant would expose the king along the rank: illegal. This is
# THE classic perft bug, because the ep capture removes two pawns from one rank
# at once and a naive pin check misses the resulting discovered attack.
8/8/8/8/k1p4R/8/3P4/3K4 w - - 0 1 ;D6 1134888
# Same idea along a diagonal.
8/8/4k3/8/2p5/8/B2P2K1/8 w - - 0 1 ;D6 1015133
# En passant capture that legally delivers check to the opponent.
8/8/1k6/2b5/2pP4/8/5K2/8 b - d3 0 1 ;D6 1440467

# --- castling legality -------------------------------------------------------
# Short castling gives check.
5k2/8/8/8/8/8/8/4K2R w K - 0 1 ;D6 661072
# Long castling gives check.
3k4/8/8/8/8/8/8/R3K3 w Q - 0 1 ;D6 803711
# Castling rights must be revoked when a rook moves or is captured.
r3k2r/1b4bq/8/8/8/8/7B/R3K2R w KQkq - 0 1 ;D4 1274206
# Castling prevented because the king would pass through an attacked square.
r3k2r/8/3Q4/8/8/5q2/8/R3K2R b KQkq - 0 1 ;D4 1720476

# --- promotion ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Promotion is the only legal way out of check.
2K2r2/4P3/8/8/8/8/8/3k4 w - - 0 1 ;D6 3821001
# Promotion that delivers check.
4k3/1P6/8/8/8/8/K7/8 w - - 0 1 ;D6 217342
# Underpromotion that delivers check - engines that only generate queen
# promotions pass every other test and fail this one.
8/P1k5/K7/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1 ;D6 92683

# --- discovered check --------------------------------------------------------
8/8/1P2K3/8/2n5/1q6/8/5k2 b - - 0 1 ;D5 1004658

# --- stalemate and checkmate detection ---------------------------------------
# Self stalemate: the side to move has no legal move and is not in check.
K1k5/8/P7/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1 ;D6 2217
# Mixed stalemate and checkmate at the leaves.
8/k1P5/8/1K6/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1 ;D7 567584
8/8/2k5/5q2/5n2/8/5K2/8 b - - 0 1 ;D4 23527
